    {
      "id": 236399,
      "name": "degausser",
      "username": "degausser",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/9fc29f/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2021-03-28T18:20:55.297Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The thing to remember about Lieutenants is that they are MUCH harder to take down than minions, so you don’t want to do a 1-on-1 conversion.  However the ‘Creator’ villain approach allows a villain to make a single lieutenant as an action, so you can, in fact, do it.  Just be careful, D12 Lieutenants can be actually more troublesome to deal with than some villains depending on how they are built.  (I built an adaptable Fragile villain that only had 10 HP+5 per PC, with four players that’s 30 HP vs, a d12 lieutenant, depending on how you roll, the Lieutenant could be harder to deal with)</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-03-28T18:20:55.297Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 20,
      "readers_count": 19,
